# Data Flow Contract
- `UI -> Provider -> Logic -> Repository -> Local (Isar) <-> Remote (API)`
- Isar is the source of truth for runtime data.

# Cache-first Rules
- Default behavior: return local/Isar data immediately when available.
- Refresh remote in the background and update local so UI updates via Isar.

# Cache Policies
- Implement cache policies with these semantics:
  - `cacheFirst`: local first, then (if needed) refresh remote
  - `networkFirst`: attempt remote first, fallback to local on failure
  - `cacheOnly`: do not call remote
  - `networkOnly`: do not use local (except as required by runtime constraints)

# Invalidation
- Invalidate/refresh cached data when remote truth changes or when policy requires it.

